Okay, so I need to figure out how to map the Agora Web SDK fields to the 15 interface features provided. Let me go through each feature one by one and see which Agora field matches or if it's missing.

Starting with feature 0: receiving rate in bits per second. The Agora field RecvBitrate is given in bps, which seems to match exactly. So I'll map feature 0 to RecvBitrate without any changes.

Feature 1 is the number of packets received. The Agora fields are receivePackets for audio and video. Since the interface requires a single source, I'll choose one, maybe RemoteVideoTrackStats, and note that it's per track. So feature 1 maps to receivePackets.

Feature 2 is number of bytes received. Agora's RecvBytes is an aggregate, so I can use that. No scaling needed, so feature 2 maps to RecvBytes.

Feature 3 is queuing delay. Looking at the Agora fields, transportDelay seems similar. It's the delay from sending to receiving, which could be related to queuing. So I'll map feature 3 to transportDelay.

Feature 4 is mean one-way delay. Agora's transportDelay is the delay between sending and receiving, which might be the one-way delay. So feature 4 maps to transportDelay as well, but I'm not entirely sure if it's mean or just a single measurement.

Feature 5 is the minimum one-way delay. Since Agora doesn't provide a specific minimum delay, this might be missing. So feature 5 is source null.

Feature 6 is delay ratio, which is mean divided by minimum. Since we don't have minimum delay, this can't be calculated. So feature 6 is missing.

Feature 7 is mean delay minus min delay. Again, without min delay, this isn't possible. So feature 7 is missing.

Feature 8 is mean packet inter-arrival time. Agora doesn't provide this directly. Maybe it's related to packet loss rate or delay, but I don't think so. So feature 8 is missing.

Feature 9 is packet jitter. Agora's downlinkNetworkQuality includes jitter, so I'll map feature 9 to that.

Feature 10 is packet loss ratio. The field currentPacketLossRate seems to fit, so feature 10 maps to that.

Feature 11 is mean lost packets per loss event. Agora has receivePacketsLost, which is the total lost packets. To find the mean, I might need to track the number of loss events, but since it's not provided, this feature is missing.

Feature 12 is share of video packets. Agora's fields don't specify the share, only the total packets. Without additional info, this is missing.

Feature 13 is share of audio packets. Same as above, can't compute the share. So missing.

Feature 14 is share of probing packets. Agora doesn't track this, so it's missing.

I think that's all the mappings. Now, I'll structure this into JSON as per the instructions.
